# Algorithms

## Detector protocol (`packages/dqt/src/dqt/algorithms/_base.py`)
```python
class Detector(Protocol):
    slug: ClassVar[str]
    group: ClassVar[str]              # matches UI tab taxonomy below
    def fit(self, reference: pd.DataFrame) -> DetectorState: ...
    def score(self, current: pd.DataFrame, state: DetectorState) -> DetectorResult: ...
```

Rule-based checks follow the same protocol with `fit()` as a no-op.

## DetectorResult
```python
@dataclass
class DetectorResult:
    score: float
    verdict: Verdict           # pass | warn | fail
    plain_english: str
    details: dict[str, Any]
```

Every detector returns this exact shape. Never return raw dicts or ad-hoc structures.

## STAT_SCALES — single source of truth
`packages/dqt/src/dqt/algorithms/_scales.py` defines `STAT_SCALES`:
```python
STAT_SCALE = (metric_slug, max, warn_threshold, fail_threshold, direction, plain_english_label, hint)
```
- Python is authoritative. Frontend reads these via `lib/stats.ts` generated by `make stats-scales`.
- **Never duplicate scales on the frontend or in tests.** Golden-file tests verify the scales themselves.
- `direction` is `"lower_is_better"` or `"higher_is_better"`.

